  "solution": {
    "text": "(i) Cassiterite contains iron and manganese tungstate, called as Wolframite.<br/><br/>They have magnetic properties.<br/><br/>(ii) Purified ore that contains 70%  <math><mtext>Sn</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>  is called black tin.<br/><br/> <math><mtext>Sn</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>→</mo><mtext>Sn</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>CO</mtext></math>  (carbon reduction)<br/><br/>(iii) Roasting is done at moderate temperature in presence of air in reverberatory furnace. Then air supply is stopped and temperature is increased to melt the mass when self<br/><br/>reduction takes place.<br/><br/>(iv) At 500 to 800K (lower temperature range in the upper part of blast furnace)<br/><br/> <math><mn>3</mn><mtext>F</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>e</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>F</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>e</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mtext>C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> <br/><br/> <math><mtext>F</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>e</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>3</mn><mtext>Fe</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mtext>C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> <br/><br/> <math><mtext>F</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>e</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>FeO</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> <br/><br/>At 900 to  <math><mn>1500</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>  (higher temperature range in the lower part of blast furnace:<br/><br/> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><mtext>C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>CO</mtext></math>  ,  <math><mtext>FeO</mtext><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>+</mo><mtext>C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
